From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: bind the VLAN of a link added by Link
 Reconfiguration

Upstream fix: hostap main 741d70dd8e32 has the same code; to be
reported upstream.

At association, ap_sta_bind_vlan() binds every partner link STA of a
non-AP MLD to its VLAN: the AP_VLAN reference, a reference to the VLAN
group of that link's authenticator (wpa_auth_sta_set_vlan()), and the
driver VLAN of the link. A link added by Link Reconfiguration got none
of this. wpa_auth_set_ml_info() points the link at its authenticator
without a group reference. Where that authenticator had no group of the
VLAN, the Link Reconfiguration Response carried the GTK of the default
group for the link. Where it had one, a later release of the link put a
reference that it never took, which freed the VLAN group of the link
while another station still used it.

Bind the added link STA alone, before the response is built. The
partner links hold their references already; ap_sta_bind_vlan() would
take a second one on each.

Do not set the driver VLAN of the added link. The driver holds one
station for the non-AP MLD, and a VLAN change moves that whole station
(mac80211 ieee80211_change_station()). The association bound it to its
interface already: the AP_VLAN, or the WDS interface of a 4-address
Multi-AP backhaul STA. A move to the VLAN interface, or to the main
interface for VLAN ID 0, would take a backhaul STA off its WDS
interface and stop its data. The WDS check of ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper()
does not catch this, because a backhaul STA gets its WDS interface at
the association without WLAN_STA_WDS.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -1897,6 +1897,7 @@ hostapd_ml_process_reconf_link(struct ho
 	}
 	wpa_auth_set_ml_info(lsta->wpa_sm, lsta->mld_assoc_link_id,
 			     &lsta->mld_info);
+	ap_sta_bind_link_vlan(lhapd, lsta);
 
 	return WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -1692,7 +1692,7 @@ void ap_sta_set_link_vlan(struct hostapd
 
 
 static int ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
-				   struct sta_info *sta)
+				   struct sta_info *sta, bool drv_set)
 {
 #ifndef CONFIG_NO_VLAN
 	const char *iface;
@@ -1768,8 +1768,10 @@ skip_counting:
 				  sta->vlan_id) < 0)
 		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "Failed to update VLAN-ID for WPA");
 
-	ret = hostapd_drv_set_sta_vlan(iface, hapd, sta->addr, sta->vlan_id,
-				       mld_link_id);
+	ret = 0;
+	if (drv_set)
+		ret = hostapd_drv_set_sta_vlan(iface, hapd, sta->addr,
+					       sta->vlan_id, mld_link_id);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		hostapd_logger(vlan_bss, sta->addr, HOSTAPD_MODULE_IEEE80211,
 			       HOSTAPD_LEVEL_DEBUG, "could not bind the STA "
@@ -1796,7 +1798,7 @@ int ap_sta_bind_vlan(struct hostapd_data
 	struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces = hapd->iface->interfaces;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
-	ret = ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(hapd, sta);
+	ret = ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(hapd, sta, true);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
@@ -1811,7 +1813,7 @@ int ap_sta_bind_vlan(struct hostapd_data
 
 		tmp_sta = ap_get_sta(tmp_hapd, sta->addr);
 		if (tmp_sta)
-			ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(tmp_hapd, tmp_sta);
+			ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(tmp_hapd, tmp_sta, true);
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
@@ -1819,6 +1821,14 @@ int ap_sta_bind_vlan(struct hostapd_data
 }
 
 
+/* The driver holds one station for a non-AP MLD, which stays on the interface
+ * that the association bound it to when a link is added. */
+int ap_sta_bind_link_vlan(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta)
+{
+	return ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(hapd, sta, false);
+}
+
+
 void ap_sta_set_sa_query_timeout(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 				 struct sta_info *sta, int value)
 {
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.h
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.h
@@ -447,6 +447,7 @@ int ap_sta_wps_cancel(struct hostapd_dat
 		      struct sta_info *sta, void *ctx);
 #endif /* CONFIG_WPS */
 int ap_sta_bind_vlan(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta);
+int ap_sta_bind_link_vlan(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta);
 int ap_sta_set_vlan(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
 		    struct vlan_description *vlan_desc);
 void ap_sta_set_link_vlan(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
